From 926defa98a5123040b2dec1b92e7725550453163 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: facetimehd downstream <facetimehd-downstream@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 12/21] v4l2: add anti-banding, switch exposure through the
 firmware

Add V4L2_CID_POWER_LINE_FREQUENCY (disabled, 50 Hz, 60 Hz) using the
firmware's flicker-frequency command, and make V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE_AUTO
start and stop the firmware's auto exposure instead of being a no-op.
Drop V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE_AUTO_PRIORITY: lowering the AE frame-rate floor
is not shown to change what the sensor delivers.

Accept control values while the channel is down instead of failing;
STREAMON replays the handler. Reject unknown controls, and support
VIDIOC_LOG_STATUS.
